{
  "nodes": [
    {
      "type": "PARAGRAPH",
      "id": "c03n0",
      "nodes": [
        {
          "type": "TEXT",
          "textData": {
            "text": "Research into light-based treatment for Hashimoto’s thyroiditis is interesting, but the device, setting and medical supervision matter. A clinical laser study cannot automatically establish what a wellness red-light panel will do for thyroid disease.",
            "decorations": []
          }
        }
      ],
      "paragraphData": {}
    },
    {
      "type": "PARAGRAPH",
      "id": "c03s1",
      "nodes": [],
      "paragraphData": {}
    },
    {
      "type": "HEADING",
      "id": "c03n1",
      "nodes": [
        {
          "type": "TEXT",
          "textData": {
            "text": "What the original trial found",
            "decorations": []
          }
        }
      ],
      "headingData": {
        "level": 2
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "PARAGRAPH",
      "id": "c03s2",
      "nodes": [],
      "paragraphData": {}
    },
    {
      "type": "PARAGRAPH",
      "id": "c03n2",
      "nodes": [
        {
          "type": "TEXT",
          "textData": {
            "text": "Höfling and colleagues studied 43 people with chronic autoimmune thyroiditis in a randomized trial. Treatment used a medical point laser with clinical follow-up. The treated group required less levothyroxine at nine months than the placebo group, and one thyroid-antibody measure improved. These findings support further research in that specific setting.",
            "decorations": []
          }
        }
      ],
      "paragraphData": {}
    },
    {
      "type": "PARAGRAPH",
      "id": "c03s3",
      "nodes": [],
      "paragraphData": {}
    },
    {
      "type": "HEADING",
      "id": "c03n3",
      "nodes": [
        {
          "type": "TEXT",
          "textData": {
            "text": "What the longer follow-up adds",
            "decorations": []
          }
        }
      ],
      "headingData": {
        "level": 2
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "PARAGRAPH",
      "id": "c03s4",
      "nodes": [],
      "paragraphData": {}
    },
    {
      "type": "PARAGRAPH",
      "id": "c03n4",
      "nodes": [
        {
          "type": "TEXT",
          "textData": {
            "text": "A later follow-up reported lower levothyroxine requirements in the previously treated group, while thyroid-antibody levels did not differ between groups. It does not establish that periodic wellness-panel sessions maintain thyroid function or prevent Hashimoto’s from progressing.",
            "decorations": []
          }
        }
      ],
      "paragraphData": {}
    },
    {
      "type": "PARAGRAPH",
      "id": "c03s5",
      "nodes": [],
      "paragraphData": {}
    },
    {
      "type": "HEADING",
      "id": "c03n5",
      "nodes": [
        {
          "type": "TEXT",
          "textData": {
            "text": "Why the equipment matters",
            "decorations": []
          }
        }
      ],
      "headingData": {
        "level": 2
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "PARAGRAPH",
      "id": "c03s6",
      "nodes": [],
      "paragraphData": {}
    },
    {
      "type": "PARAGRAPH",
      "id": "c03n6",
      "nodes": [
        {
          "type": "TEXT",
          "textData": {
            "text": "“Red light” describes a broad category. A directed laser and a broad LED panel can differ in output, treatment area and delivered dose. Similar wavelength labels do not make their results interchangeable. The cited studies do not provide a validated home-panel or Matrix-session protocol for treating the thyroid.",
            "decorations": []
          }
        }
      ],
      "paragraphData": {}
    },
    {
      "type": "PARAGRAPH",
      "id": "c03s7",
      "nodes": [],
      "paragraphData": {}
    },
    {
      "type": "PARAGRAPH",
      "id": "c03n7",
      "nodes": [
        {
          "type": "TEXT",
          "textData": {
            "text": "For that reason, this article does not give a thyroid exposure schedule, treatment distance or minutes per thyroid lobe. Those would be medical treatment instructions that the panel evidence here does not establish.",
            "decorations": []
          }
        }
      ],
      "paragraphData": {}
    },
    {
      "type": "PARAGRAPH",
      "id": "c03s8",
      "nodes": [],
      "paragraphData": {}
    },
    {
      "type": "HEADING",
      "id": "c03n8",
      "nodes": [
        {
          "type": "TEXT",
          "textData": {
            "text": "What this means for your care",
            "decorations": []
          }
        }
      ],
      "headingData": {
        "level": 2
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "PARAGRAPH",
      "id": "c03s9",
      "nodes": [],
      "paragraphData": {}
    },
    {
      "type": "PARAGRAPH",
      "id": "c03n9",
      "nodes": [
        {
          "type": "TEXT",
          "textData": {
            "text": "Keep thyroid testing and medication decisions with your prescribing clinician. Do not reduce or stop thyroid medication based on a wellness session, symptoms alone or this article. If you are interested in clinical light-based thyroid research, discuss the actual papers and their limitations with your endocrinologist.",
            "decorations": []
          }
        }
      ],
      "paragraphData": {}
    },
    {
